    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443-a4">

                <pb facs="0867" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg743"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    121.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">discussion.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Monitor Republicano, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1880-10-13">October 13,
                        1880</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Long and violent has been the discussion caused in the Senate by the note of the
                    executive asking permission for American troops to cross the frontiers.</p>
                <pb facs="0868" n="744" xml:id="pg744"/>
                <p>We hope the good Mexicans who are in that chamber will not give their approbation
                    to the complacent request of the cabinet, because, as we are informed, it is
                    very dangerous for Mexico.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
